    "## Problem 1: Nucleotide Frequency Counter\n",
    "Given a DNA sequence string, build a dictionary named nucleotide_counts that stores the frequency of each base ('A', 'C', 'G', 'T').\n",
    "Input data:\n",
    "    dna_seq = \"AGCTTTTCATTCTGACTGCAACGGGCAATATGTCTCTGTGTGGATTAAAAAAAGAGTGTCTGATAGCAGC\"\n",
    "Tasks:\n",
    "* Initialize an empty dictionary or build it using a comprehension.\n",
    "* Count how many times each nucleotide appears in dna_seq.\n",
    "* Store each count under its respective uppercase base key ('A', 'C', 'G', 'T')."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "23fd858a-7abd-4f62-ab67-8523a8d9bd01",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "{'A': 20, 'C': 12, 'G': 17, 'T': 21}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "dna_seq = \"AGCTTTTCATTCTGACTGCAACGGGCAATATGTCTCTGTGTGGATTAAAAAAAGAGTGTCTGATAGCAGC\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# {key: value for item}\n",
    "nucleotide_counts = {base: dna_seq.count(base) for base in \"ACGT\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(nucleotide_counts)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a7a267ef-19b3-4670-8dd2-a18beb618be6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Problem 2: GC-Content Classifier\n",
    "Calculate the GC-content percentage for a list of DNA reads and filter for high-GC sequences (>50%).\n",
    "Input data:\n",
    "    reads = [\"ATGCATGC\", \"GCGCGCGC\", \"ATATATAT\", \"CGGCGGAT\", \"TTATATAA\"]\n",
    "Tasks:\n",
    "* Write a function or comprehension that calculates the GC percentage: ((Count of G + Count of C)/ Total length) * 100\n",
    "* Filter the list to include only reads where the GC content is strictly greater than 50.0%.\n",
    "* Store the result in a dictionary named high_gc_reads where the key is the sequence and the value is its rounded GC percentage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "322d2d41-e02b-4ee4-9f44-d4590d58b883",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "{'GCGCGCGC': 100.0, 'CGGCGGAT': 75.0}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "reads = [\"ATGCATGC\", \"GCGCGCGC\", \"ATATATAT\", \"CGGCGGAT\", \"TTATATAA\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Let's write and define a function that calculates the GC %\n",
    "def calc_gc(seq):\n",
    "    return ((seq.count(\"G\") + seq.count(\"C\")) / len(seq)) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "# Let's build the dictionary. Loop through each read one by one.\n",
    "high_gc_reads = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "for read in reads:\n",
    "    if calc_gc(read) > 50.0:\n",
    "        high_gc_reads[read] = round(calc_gc(read), 1)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(high_gc_reads)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dd3f877f-405a-4d37-ba75-55d69d2f644d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Problem 3: FASTQ Header Parser\n",
    "Process raw sequencing header strings to extract metadata into a structured dictionary.\n",
    "Input data:\n",
    "    headers = [\n",
    "    \"SEQ01_len150_QCpass\",\n",
    "    \"SEQ02_len75_QCfail\",\n",
    "    \"SEQ03_len150_QCpass\",\n",
    "    \"SEQ04_len100_QCpass\",\n",
    "    \"SEQ05_len50_QCfail\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "Tasks:\n",
    "* Use comprehension to filter out only headers ending with QCpass.\n",
    "* Split the string to isolate the sample name (e.g., 'SEQ01') and add the integer length (e.g., 150).\n",
    "* Create a dictionary named passing_qc mapping each passing sample name to its length as an integer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "id": "c309dc90-74e1-4db7-a755-0947118272ee",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "{'SEQ01': 150, 'SEQ03': 150, 'SEQ04': 100}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "headers = [\n",
    "    \"SEQ01_len150_QCpass\",\n",
    "    \"SEQ02_len75_QCfail\",\n",
    "    \"SEQ03_len150_QCpass\",\n",
    "    \"SEQ04_len100_QCpass\",\n",
    "    \"SEQ05_len50_QCfail\"\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "passing_qc = {\n",
    "    h.split(\"_\")[0]: int(h.split(\"_\")[1].replace(\"len\", \"\"))\n",
    "    for h in headers\n",
    "    if h.endswith(\"QCpass\")\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print(passing_qc)"
   ]
  }
